        {
          "ruleId": "CODE INJECTION",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Remote Code Execution via Function Constructor in Custom Rate Formula Evaluation: Data Path Analysis:\n- Source: In `services/credit-service/src/index.js`, the endpoint `POST /api/v1/credit/proposals/:id/evaluate-formula` parses incoming JSON payload without authentication and extracts `body.formula`.\n- Sanitization/Validation: `evaluateCustomRateFormula` only verifies `if (!formula || typeof formula !== 'string')`. There is no sandboxing, AST parsing, or whitelist of allowable mathematical operations.\n- Sink: At line 60 of `contract_engine.js`, the untrusted string is interpolated directly into `new Function('amount', 'term', 'score', `return (${formula});`)` and immediately invoked.\n\nConceptual Exploit Payload:\nSend an HTTP POST request to evaluate a custom formula containing arbitrary Node.js code execution:\n```http\nPOST /api/v1/credit/proposals/prop_101/evaluate-formula HTTP/1.1\nHost: localhost:8084\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{\n  \"formula\": \"process.mainModule.require('child_process').execSync('id').toString()\",\n  \"context\": {\n    \"amount\": 1000,\n    \"term\": 12,\n    \"score\": 750\n  }\n}\n```\nThe constructor runs the injected JavaScript in the current process context, leading to Remote Code Execution (RCE)."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "services/credit-service/src/services/contract_engine.js"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 59,
                  "endLine": 61
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
