        {
          "ruleId": "PROTOTYPE POLLUTION",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Prototype Pollution via Unsanitized Object Key Recursion in deepMerge: Data Path Analysis:\n- Source: In `services/identity-service/src/index.js`, the endpoint `PATCH /api/v1/customers/:id/profile` receives untrusted JSON updates from the request body and forwards them to `customerStore.updateProfile(customerId, body)`.\n- Sanitization/Validation: `deepMerge` does not filter dangerous keys such as `__proto__`, `constructor`, or `prototype`.\n- Sink: When `key` is `\"__proto__\"`, accessing `target[key]` evaluates to `Object.prototype`. The recursive call `deepMerge(target[key], val)` then assigns properties directly onto `Object.prototype` at line 18 (`target[key] = val`), polluting global prototype properties across the Node.js runtime.\n\nConceptual Exploit Payload:\nSend an HTTP PATCH request with a crafted JSON payload targeting `__proto__`:\n```http\nPATCH /api/v1/customers/cust_001/profile HTTP/1.1\nHost: localhost:8082\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{\n  \"__proto__\": {\n    \"polluted\": true,\n    \"isAdmin\": true\n  }\n}\n```\nFollowing this request, `({}).polluted === true` and `({}).isAdmin === true` in the application environment, allowing authorization bypass, denial of service, or further exploitation."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
