          "ruleId": "Concurrent Execution using Shared Resource with Improper Synchronization",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Check-Then-Set Race Condition in Payment Idempotency Processing: Data Path Analysis:\n- Source: In `services/payments-service/main.py`, endpoint `POST /api/v1/payments/pix` receives `Idempotency-Key` via request headers or JSON payload and passes it to `payment_svc.process_pix_payment`.\n- Sanitization/Validation: At line 85, the service checks whether the key exists in the cache (`cached = self.idempotency_mgr.get_record(idempotency_key)`). However, no lock is acquired, and the transaction is not reserved or locked in a \"PENDING/PROCESSING\" state before external settlement.\n- Sink: Lines 104-130: After the check, execution delays for downstream rail simulation (`time.sleep(0.01)`), and the record is only committed to the idempotency store *after* the payment settlement finishes. If two concurrent payment requests arrive with the same `Idempotency-Key`, both find the key unset in cache, both proceed to execute payment settlement, and both produce separate settled transaction orders (`pay_...`), defeating the idempotency guarantee.\n\nConceptual Exploit Payload:\nSend two parallel requests with the identical `Idempotency-Key`:\n```http\nPOST /api/v1/payments/pix HTTP/1.1\nHost: localhost:8083\nContent-Type: application/json\nIdempotency-Key: idem_race_attack_01\n\n{\n  \"sourceAccountId\": \"acc_1001\",\n  \"pixKey\": \"merchant@store.com\",\n  \"amount\": 500.0,\n  \"description\": \"Payment\"\n}\n```\nDue to the check-then-set race window between lines 85 and 130, both requests execute settlement independently, creating two distinct payment orders and double-charging the account."
