          "ruleId": "Improper Enforcement of Behavioral Workflow",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Missing State Machine Transition Guard in Credit Proposal Lifecycle: Data Path Analysis:\n- Source: In `services/credit-service/src/index.js`, route `PATCH /api/v1/credit/proposals/:id/status` accepts JSON input with `body.status` and `body.reason` and invokes `proposalStore.updateStatus(id, body.status, body.reason)`.\n- Sanitization/Validation: `updateStatus` only checks `if (proposal.status === 'CANCELLED')`. It contains no state-machine transition guard validation to enforce that a proposal must progress from `DRAFT` -\u003e `ANALYSIS_PENDING` -\u003e `APPROVED` -\u003e `CONTRACT_SIGNED` before reaching `DISBURSEMENT_READY`.\n- Sink: Lines 119-126 overwrite `proposal.status = newStatus` and persist it. A borrower or unauthenticated caller can arbitrarily transition a brand new or unapproved credit proposal straight to `DISBURSEMENT_READY`, bypassing underwriting and credit committee approval.\n\nConceptual Exploit Payload:\nSend an HTTP PATCH request to update the status of a pending proposal:\n```http\nPATCH /api/v1/credit/proposals/prop_102/status HTTP/1.1\nHost: localhost:8084\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{\n  \"status\": \"DISBURSEMENT_READY\",\n  \"reason\": \"Bypassed underwriting checks\"\n}\n```\nThe server accepts the transition and returns status 200 with `status: \"DISBURSEMENT_READY\"`, qualifying the proposal for immediate loan disbursement."
