          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Concurrency Race Condition (TOCTOU) Allowing Double-Spending in Account Debit: Data Path Analysis:\n- Source: HTTP POST endpoint `/api/v1/accounts/debit` handled in `services/core-banking/internal/handler/http.go:HandleDebit` reads JSON input (`accountId`, `amount`, `description`, `referenceId`) and calls `bankingSvc.Debit()`.\n- Sanitization/Validation: At lines 97-100, the method checks `if acc.Balance \u003c amount`. However, this read-and-check operation is performed without acquiring a mutex or performing an atomic database compare-and-swap / transaction isolation lock.\n- Sink: At line 103, an artificial ledger delay `time.Sleep(15 * time.Millisecond)` occurs between reading the balance and updating it (`newBalance := acc.Balance - amount`, `s.repo.UpdateAccount(acc)`). Because Go's HTTP server handles each request in a concurrent goroutine, multiple requests sent in parallel can pass the liquidity check before any one request commits the deducted balance, causing double-spending and draining account balances beyond allowed limits.\n\nConceptual Exploit Payload:\nSend two or more concurrent HTTP requests in parallel for an account with balance 1250.00:\n```http\nPOST /api/v1/accounts/debit HTTP/1.1\nHost: localhost:8081\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{\n  \"accountId\": \"acc_1002\",\n  \"amount\": 1000.0,\n  \"description\": \"Exploit Debit 1\",\n  \"referenceId\": \"ref_race_1\"\n}\n```\nand concurrently:\n```http\nPOST /api/v1/accounts/debit HTTP/1.1\nHost: localhost:8081\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{\n  \"accountId\": \"acc_1002\",\n  \"amount\": 1000.0,\n  \"description\": \"Exploit Debit 2\",\n  \"referenceId\": \"ref_race_2\"\n}\n```\nBoth goroutines observe `acc.Balance == 1250.0 \u003e= 1000.0` during the 15ms window, and both proceed to debit, resulting in a total of 2000.0 debited from an account holding only 1250.0."
